# Fork production build flags — tracked so every checkout/worktree bakes them in.
# Non-secret.
#
# VITE_THUNDERBOLT_CLOUD_URL is one name for every deployment: the customer points
# it at their own backend with an internal DNS zone on exactly this FQDN (or a
# hosts entry), so one build serves all of them instead of one build per customer.
# There is deliberately NO public A record — in a closed perimeter external DNS is
# unreachable anyway, and the absence makes a misconfigured client fail loudly
# instead of silently reaching someone else's host with its tokens.
# `.local` would have been wrong here: RFC 6762 reserves it for mDNS, so the query
# never reaches the corporate resolver, and no CA will issue for it.
#
# Deployment side: dev-local/docker/README-pilot-tls.md.
# NOTE: the value is persisted in localStorage, so an upgrade over an existing
# install keeps whatever address it first saw — see the same runbook.
VITE_THUNDERBOLT_CLOUD_URL="https://backend.volt.oktaplus.ru/v1"
VITE_AUTH_ENABLE_ANONYMOUS=true
VITE_BYPASS_WAITLIST="true"
